NUMUTILS - Numerical Utilities Library
======================================
Version 1.2.3
Released: 2005-03-15

NUMUTILS is a lightweight numerical computing library providing
common algorithms for scientific and engineering applications.

FEATURES
--------
- Basic statistics (mean, variance, stddev, median, percentiles)
- Array sorting and manipulation
- Matrix operations (create, free, determinant, LU decomposition, multiply)
- Interpolation (linear and cubic)
- Root finding (bisection and Newton-Raphson methods)
- Numerical integration (trapezoid and Simpson's rules)
- Random number generation (uniform and normal distributions)
- Correlation and covariance

BUILDING
--------
Requirements:
- GCC 3.x or 4.x
- GNU Make

To build the static library:
  $ make

To build the shared library:
  $ make shared

INSTALLATION
------------
As root:
  $ make install          # for static library
  $ make install-shared   # for shared library

This installs:
- libnumutils.a or libnumutils.so to /usr/local/lib
- numutils.h to /usr/local/include

USAGE
-----
Include the header:
  #include <numutils.h>

Link with:
  $ gcc myprogram.c -lnumutils -lm

TESTING
--------
A test program is provided in the parent directory:
  $ gcc test_numutils.c -lnumutils -lm -o test_numutils
  $ ./test_numutils

